      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T11:11:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I realized that CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator does not use ConnectivityService handler thread.\n`synchronized (mNetworkRequests)` does not work here since other code does not acquire lock to access mNetworkRequests.\nI think there are two solutions.\n\n1) Update CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator to use ConnectivityService handler thread.\nBy doing this, onCarrierPrivilegesLost should run on ConnectivityService handler thread and you don\u0027t need to worry about the race.\n\n2) Update onCarrierPrivilegesLost to post message to ConnectivityService handler and go through mNetworkRequests from the handler thread.\n\nThe first solution is ideal but require some refactoring in CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator.\nI think you can implement 2nd solution with TODO comment for the first solution.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1281,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 1281,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "0a6b6deb664c16fb134b8762965042a7dae201cc",
